#: ../../source/quality/performance.md:1 572543f0e9f649b2ad8274c603446f7e
msgid "Performance Architecture & Benchmarks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:43 539af3ac3309414eb669ca5c8ccf0ced
msgid ""
"This document outlines the performance characteristics, benchmarking "
"architecture, and baseline performance metrics for `findfmt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:48 5af88830549341d6b1cd1ea30c95c67f
msgid "1. Performance Goals & Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:50 a539897b9ac448e58fa42b3c1562e3fb
msgid ""
"`findfmt` is engineered to deliver high-throughput filesystem traversal "
"and intelligent content classification across large codebases and "
"monorepos (>100,000 files)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:53 e9d98967fa124f24b1d718f5ffd26921
msgid "The performance model focuses on three primary metrics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:55 25c0d188251b41148f73e32f560f6c88
msgid ""
"**Traversal Throughput (files/sec and dirs/sec)**: Maximizing file "
"discovery and content inspection throughput across large repository "
"hierarchies while pruning excluded trees early via `.gitignore` "
"specifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:59 a6cccd9f7e514c16baaa3fc93c690aa8
msgid ""
"**Latency to First Yielded Result (TTFR)**: Measuring first-byte "
"responsiveness (in milliseconds) from execution start until the first "
"matching item is yielded. Low TTFR is critical for pipe streaming and "
"interactive subshells."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:63 fb7cca85e2f34d29a3fd236498dcaf51
msgid ""
"**Peak Heap Memory Footprint**: Tracking peak heap memory allocation "
"using Python's `tracemalloc` standard library to ensure low, bounded "
"memory usage during multi-level directory traversal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:68 f7d17cc0d1b64a0b89e0eab8abb35d83
msgid "2. Core Optimization Vectors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:70 a1f39672c8b2480da051de8f575c659f
msgid ""
"The traversal and classification pipeline incorporates several targeted "
"optimizations to maximize throughput across large repository hierarchies:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:73 79f971b7f4d84d1d8bcaae7d7ba8418e
msgid "2.1. Redundant Syscalls & `Path.resolve()` Elimination"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:75 79d44d5265cf43369a4b5dc4d0229d6e
msgid ""
"Earlier implementations resolved relative paths by invoking "
"`Path.resolve()` on every discovered file. In deep directory structures, "
"resolving paths generates tens of thousands of redundant `readlink` and "
"`stat` system calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:79 39419acba25a4224b03796b32b1ae9c6
msgid ""
"`findfmt` optimizes this by computing directory-relative paths with "
"`os.path.relpath()` and prefix operations derived from pre-computed root "
"strings. File classification operates on the entry's original path "
"without resolving symlinks for regular files, avoiding per-file link "
"resolution overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:84 1bb1ba364f08462392c3d1647c8304cb
msgid "2.2. `DirEntry` Metadata Preservation & Single-Buffer Content Reads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:86 cc44d1e8e6ab453ea5d7c987844e138e
msgid ""
"Python's `os.scandir()` yields `os.DirEntry` objects whose cached file "
"type (`is_file`, `is_dir`, `is_symlink`) and `stat()` attributes are "
"populated directly from the operating system's directory stream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:90 dc9c60190b6143b18d9e7b0f958c2e3e
msgid ""
"`findfmt` preserves and forwards `os.DirEntry` instances throughout "
"traversal and classification:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:92 dca61913b5a44ecfb304113c9f6c359a
msgid ""
"**Zero-Stat Verification**: Avoids secondary `os.stat()` syscalls by "
"reusing cached entry metadata."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:94 d874d40328e64ca882acd94608e5296f
msgid ""
"**Single-Buffer Content Inspection**: When content inspection is required"
" (for shebang or MIME detection), `findfmt` reads an initial buffer (the "
"first 2,048 to 4,096 bytes) once into memory. This buffer is shared "
"across shebang parsing, MIME type sniffing, and tag classification, "
"eliminating duplicate `open()` and `read()` syscalls on candidate files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:99 794e31d7d74249468be83c6d1266529e
msgid "2.3. Zero-Allocation Gitignore Rule Matching Hot Loop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:101 8a793eaa32b54f05a5b4cafec4694404
msgid "In traversal loops evaluating multiple active `.gitignore` specifications:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:103 3fe76b93580b4bcbbcf3cd4281de761b
msgid ""
"Path operations avoid redundant `Path.is_relative_to()` and "
"`Path.relative_to()` allocations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:104 34aa986789074f17bf8b6e9ebbc6bc71
msgid ""
"Relative path representations are passed as normalized strings, "
"leveraging fast string prefix matching to evaluate directory boundaries "
"and pruning rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:107 5338cc76111346118c322c9d7fa5aba4
msgid "2.4. Fast-Path Filter Short-Circuiting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:109 65e46aa71487438783df7efa57712b6e
msgid "When specific tags are requested (for example, `--tag python`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:111 65fe5343e6de423887712d95e9d0e2ca
msgid ""
"`can_skip_file_by_tags()` inspects the filename extension before opening "
"the file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:112 8a1ac2bbb5204f5b9e1ebd5c66552b8e
msgid ""
"If an extension definitively excludes the requested tags and indicates no"
" executable shebang is possible (such as known binary formats or fixed "
"non-script extensions), the file read is bypassed entirely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:118 729c3431cc344522bc73631c2f73b40e
msgid "3. Parallel Batch Execution & Concurrency Analysis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:120 39b313d1c345425f931fa7f8b8f46733
msgid ""
"Parallelizing the content-inspection phase using "
"`concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor` was evaluated against the "
"streaming generator architecture on modern multi-core NVMe systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:123 10fcd39f6b8b420f8a50134e0fbddd58
msgid "3.1. ThreadPoolExecutor vs. Streaming Generator Benchmarks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:125 a28d514a78774e4d8912cbe89fa79147
msgid ""
"Empirical profiling evaluated a 4-worker `ThreadPoolExecutor` against the"
" sequential streaming generator across a test suite of 1,000 files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:128 604aa6d6f78e42e1bc6c8f36c62c38a2
msgid ""
"**Sequential Streaming Generator**: Processed 1,000 files in 0.0584 "
"seconds (~17,131 files/second)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:130 146bcd52c4184fa2bcc1795aa59083e3
msgid ""
"**ThreadPoolExecutor (4 Workers)**: Processed 1,000 files in 0.1076 "
"seconds (~9,295 files/second)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:132 256da27c56844e558f4c6bcdf8934507
msgid ""
"Multi-threading introduced an approximate 1.84x slowdown compared to the "
"single-threaded implementation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:135 045a1eca527a469a987f323ded9f91f0
msgid "3.2. Concurrency Trade-Off Rationale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:137 ceb31747e1e043aca8062eef7b4a25d7
msgid ""
"Several architectural factors explain why single-threaded traversal "
"outperforms thread pools for local filesystem inspection in Python:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:140 33adfbb9e7cb40b68d827bde3a09a5d0
msgid ""
"**OS Page Cache & SSD Latency**: Reading initial file buffers (2 KB) from"
" modern NVMe storage and operating system page caches executes in "
"microseconds. I/O wait times are negligible compared to thread scheduling"
" costs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:143 7d2ea91a1f1f4591ba1e81e7425c7b6a
msgid ""
"**GIL Contention & Dispatch Overhead**: Submitting tasks to thread pools,"
" queuing futures, context switching, and Global Interpreter Lock (GIL) "
"contention in CPython introduce synchronization overhead that dwarfs the "
"cost of reading small file headers sequentially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:146 5ebc8b2800af49df96e42d0f9fac862f
msgid ""
"**Time-to-First-Result (TTFR) Degradation**: Batch thread dispatching "
"chunks results, delaying initial yields. The single-threaded generator "
"yields matching entries immediately (sub-millisecond TTFR), which is "
"essential for interactive subshells and piping into tools like `fzf` or "
"`head`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:150 66830b9ca0094749b5eceb39c2171fb0
msgid ""
"**Bounded Memory Guarantees**: A pure generator maintains constant "
"memory, whereas parallel thread pools accumulate collections of pending "
"futures and buffers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:153 5dc5809df24b41d5a19ca344dfb48922
msgid ""
"Based on these empirical results, `findfmt` retains its single-threaded "
"streaming generator design as the optimal performance architecture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:158 555324dee32c4a7a9b98bc882ac40b82
msgid "4. Automated Benchmark Harness (`tools/benchmark.py`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:160 0e6d924a181b436ebd178e2bd39e99f6
msgid ""
"The repository includes a dedicated, automated benchmark suite at "
"`tools/benchmark.py` that generates reproducible synthetic datasets and "
"measures traversal performance across standard tiers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:163 46d2383125fb476cbe403efb2f5bbb74
msgid "4.1. Tiered Datasets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:165 a98c7d7b15224d3ba837fac108feabf3
msgid ""
"The harness supports three standardized dataset tiers alongside custom "
"directory targeting:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:167 be213fec606b4583a9fbc7ce5541004c
msgid ""
"**Small Tier (\\<1,000 files)**: Generates approximately 800 files across"
" nested directories with `.gitignore` exclusion rules. Designed for fast "
"local feedback (\\<1 second execution)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:170 c2fe90fca6b447d3a3912c12c5527f02
msgid ""
"**Medium Tier (10,000–50,000 files)**: Generates approximately 12,000 "
"files across multiple package subtrees, simulating standard enterprise "
"codebases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:173 f9f8dd4f33b9410c9effa1aae5d68a2f
msgid ""
"**Monorepo Tier (>100,000 files)**: Stress test dataset simulating large "
"monorepo structures with deep hierarchies and mixed file types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:176 2eef738718534a5eaaeaee1b06ac93d7
msgid ""
"**Custom Directory Target (`-d, --target-dir`)**: Benchmarks real-world "
"directory trees directly, such as the `findfmt` repository or user-"
"specified projects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:179 1f71f0c9624e4d7785cbe9b2d0150206
msgid "4.1.1. Deterministic Reproducibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:181 bba25e03e78c4e87ad0c57208ffe66bd
msgid ""
"Synthetic trees are generated deterministically using a fixed random seed"
" (`--seed 42` by default). The generator constructs realistic directory "
"trees with diverse file extensions (`.py`, `.sh`, `.md`, `.json`, "
"`.yaml`, `.txt`, `.bin`), executable scripts without extensions "
"containing shebang headers, and root `.gitignore` exclusion "
"specifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:186 3dcc5afc55b44ba09b4014916b1ec004
msgid "4.2. Filesystem Topologies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:188 63833346feee44d899b7e5f130376012
msgid ""
"To model realistic disk structures, the benchmark harness supports "
"representative topologies via `--topology` (`-T`):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:191 0b40f3ddabb7408cb3e32f7bddd804ae
msgid ""
"**Standard (`standard`)**: A balanced multi-tier package tree (60 "
"directories) simulating a typical project directory hierarchy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:193 dce0fcb5f4fc4174a04e20cca0019e88
msgid ""
"**Flat (`flat`)**: A single directory containing all generated files (for"
" example, 10,000 files in one folder), isolating raw directory stream "
"parsing throughput from recursive traversal overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:195 ca489b13e62247f2afc833433b2783af
msgid ""
"**Deep (`deep`)**: A deeply nested hierarchy (20 levels of nesting with a"
" branching factor of 2), testing recursion depth limits, call-stack "
"efficiency, and path concatenation overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:197 489eb37956b84edcb6c0948284fe6d33
msgid ""
"**Real-World Monorepo (`real-world`)**: A realistic monorepo topology "
"featuring multiple sub-projects alongside massive ignored directories "
"(`node_modules/`, `.venv/`, `dist/`, `build/`) containing thousands of "
"excluded files, verifying early `.gitignore` directory pruning efficiency"
" in $O(1)$ time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:202 eb7ab94267024281851924eae1326d75
msgid "4.3. Output Formatters & Classification Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:204 82c5f162d41c4e85bf5c152c2f25b197
msgid ""
"The harness benchmarks output formatting throughput, streaming "
"efficiency, and Time-to-First-Result (TTFR) latency via `--format` (`-F`)"
" and `--list-tags`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:207 47a8eeeb384145629c5cea0aab1210b7
msgid ""
"**Streaming Formats (`text`, `jsonl`, `tsv`, `csv`)**: Streams entries "
"lazily directly to the sink without buffering matching inventories into "
"RAM, maintaining bounded $O(1)$ heap overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:209 8ae68582de6a44c4b2df7878323c54f4
msgid ""
"**Buffered Formats (`json`, `tree`, `table`)**: Ingests all matching "
"records before building structured trees or serialized tabular "
"representations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../performance.md:211 b3dd372c2b934eb2b32c6002768fe233
msgid ""
"**Tag & MIME Inspection (`--list-tags`)**: Measures content inspection "
"overhead when resolving MIME classifications and tag metadata across "
"discovered files."
msgstr ""

